issue_context.body:
**Context:**
- Playwright Version: 1.22.2
- Operating System: win 10
- Node.js version: 16.6.2
- Browser: Chromium

<!-- CLI to auto-capture this info -->
<!-- npx envinfo --preset playwright --markdown -->

**Code Snippet**

```javascript
const {chromium, webkit, firefox} = require('playwright');

(async () => {
	const browser = await chromium.launch()
	const context = await browser.newContext()
	const page = await context.newPage()

	await page.setContent(`
	<div>
	  …
	</div>
	`)

	test.describe('First describe', () => {
		test.beforeAll(async () => {
			console.log('Before test')
		})
		test.afterAll(async () => {
			console.log('After test') // won't be executed
		})

		test.describe('Second describe', () => {
			test('First test', async () => {
				console.log('First test')
				expect(1).toEqual(1)
			})
			test.skip('Second test', async () => {
				console.log('Second test')
				expect(1).toEqual(1)
			})
		})
	})
})()
```

**Describe the bug**

If last test of the describe has attribute `.skip` then `.AfterAll` block won't be executed. If you move test with `.skip` up and last test won't have this attribute then `.AfterAll` block will work.

comments:
Just wanted to add I ran into this same issue too.  When the last file in a test is .skip the after all is ignored. Below is another contrived example, but also when ran in a test.describe.serial it does the same thing.



## Context:
Playwright Version: 1.22.2
Operating System: win 10
Node version: 16.13.2
Browser: Chromium

## Code Snippet Broken
_Output_
before all
t1

```
import {test} from '@playwright/test';


test.beforeAll(async () => {
  console.log("before all");
});

test.afterAll(async () => {
  console.log("after all");
});

test(`basic test1`, async () => {
  console.log("t1");
});

test.skip(`basic test2`, async () => {
  console.log("t2");
});
```


## Code Snippet Working As Expected
_Output_ 
before all
t1
t3
after all

```
import {test} from '@playwright/test';


test.beforeAll(async () => {
  console.log("before all");
});

test.afterAll(async () => {
  console.log("after all");
});

test(`basic test1`, async () => {
  console.log("t1");
});

test.skip(`basic test2`, async () => {
  console.log("t2");
});

test(`basic test3`, async ({ page }) => {
  console.log("t3");
});

```
